cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this design, its GDSII results, or its measurement data, please cite it as below. Code is licensed under Apache-2.0; hardware (RTL and GDSII) under CERN-OHL-P-2.0."
title: "SHA-256 Accelerator: zero-cost open-source tapeout on SkyWater sky130A with OpenLane"
abstract: >-
  A single-block SHA-256 compression core taken from Verilog to GDSII with OpenLane 1.1.1 and the
  SkyWater sky130A PDK, at zero commercial-EDA and zero fabrication cost. Six generations of
  iteration are included: v1 parallel I/O, v2 32-bit serial interface with a two-stage pipeline,
  v3 three-stage pipeline, v4 die shrink to 640x640 um, v5 clock-constraint correction to 26 ns
  (three PVT corners closed, 38.46 MHz), and v6 pushed to 24 ns (41.67 MHz, three corners still
  closed, tightest setup margin +1.25 ns). v1-v4 are reported as failing timing signoff, as measured.
  Includes per-generation GDSII, metrics, three-corner STA reports, Magic-vs-KLayout XOR results,
  and scripts to re-run functional simulation and synthesis checks.
